  "premise_review": [
    "The full local structure contains the exact ModularityContract and HasseWeilContract packages, followed by two supplied arrows from modularity.associated into the two exact HasseWeil propositions. No field is dropped and no independently chosen bare Prop is introduced by this local record.",
    "Both genuine theorem proofs are exact applications of their corresponding stored implication to the full supplied B and h : B.modularity.associated. Neither proves modularity, constructs a curve/L-function, or derives analytic continuation/functional equations without the stored implication.",
    "The complete original ArithmeticBoundary context was read. associated, hasAnalyticContinuation and hasFunctionalEquation are arbitrary Prop fields in those external contracts, with stored certification witnesses. They are not definitions of a modular-form association, analytic extension or functional equation. The Curve/LFunction/ModularForm carriers are independent fields with no new equality or connection imposed here.",
    "A coherent supplied-implication package is retained whole with both closely related consequence theorems. Splitting away either carrier/contract package would change the dependent field types, and no historical provider alias or replacement is introduced.",
    "Only containing namespace scaffolding changes. The exact original import and open Research.ArithmeticBoundary remain; explicit open Folder restores the original relative namespace lookup under the new GRWTSK namespace. That compatibility remains static/unreplayed.",
    "The source contract-boundary documentation and research claims remain exact as source provenance; no kernel acceptance, mathematical completion, original-authorship determination or analytic bridge is asserted by this review."
